\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Answers and grounding profiles on real annotation (E7).} (\textbf  {A})~For every GO term with at least $20$ member genes, the share of members whose membership has no experimental ground (\textsf  {icon}{} or \textsf  {collapsed}), terms ranked. Medians: human $0.59$ ($2{,}275$ terms), yeast $0.32$ ($498$), \emph  {Arabidopsis} $0.74$ ($1{,}122$). A gene-set file returns the same members for each term. (\textbf  {B})~Profiles of the answer ``variants classified pathogenic in gene X'' for the fifteen genes with most such variants. \emph  {TTN} answers are $99\%$ \textsf  {index}; \emph  {BRCA2} $53\%$ \textsf  {index}, $42\%$ \textsf  {composite}, $5\%$ \textsf  {icon}; \emph  {LDLR} $46\%$ \textsf  {index}, $38\%$ \textsf  {composite}, $16\%$ \textsf  {icon}. (\textbf  {C})~Claimed minus true index share (contact witness present) of the $387{,}523$ pathogenic ClinVar variants, when each submission's collection method is emitted with probability $k$ and a contact method is fabricated for variants without one with probability $f$. Incomplete emission understates (to $-0.94$), fabrication overstates (to $+0.06$, the whole remaining share), and the answer rows are identical everywhere (\Cref  {prop:directions}). (\textbf  {D})~Verdict information per record and the part each receiver keeps: the GO annotation file keeps all $1.74$ bits of human memberships, a gene-set file none; ClinVar submissions keep $0.20$ bits, VCF-style fields $0.08$.}}{18}{figure.caption.24}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:p7}{{7}{18}{\textbf {Answers and grounding profiles on real annotation (E7).} (\textbf {A})~For every GO term with at least $20$ member genes, the share of members whose membership has no experimental ground (\vico {} or \vcol ), terms ranked. Medians: human $0.59$ ($2{,}275$ terms), yeast $0.32$ ($498$), \emph {Arabidopsis} $0.74$ ($1{,}122$). A gene-set file returns the same members for each term. (\textbf {B})~Profiles of the answer ``variants classified pathogenic in gene X'' for the fifteen genes with most such variants. \emph {TTN} answers are $99\%$ \vind ; \emph {BRCA2} $53\%$ \vind , $42\%$ \vcom , $5\%$ \vico ; \emph {LDLR} $46\%$ \vind , $38\%$ \vcom , $16\%$ \vico . (\textbf {C})~Claimed minus true index share (contact witness present) of the $387{,}523$ pathogenic ClinVar variants, when each submission's collection method is emitted with probability $k$ and a contact method is fabricated for variants without one with probability $f$. Incomplete emission understates (to $-0.94$), fabrication overstates (to $+0.06$, the whole remaining share), and the answer rows are identical everywhere (\Cref {prop:directions}). (\textbf {D})~Verdict information per record and the part each receiver keeps: the GO annotation file keeps all $1.74$ bits of human memberships, a gene-set file none; ClinVar submissions keep $0.20$ bits, VCF-style fields $0.08$}{figure.caption.24}{}}
